# Agentia CLI

Use Agentia to manage Copado work items. Prefer registered Agentia MCP tools; otherwise use the CLI with `--json`.

Authentication must be configured before operational commands. Never print credentials, tokens, or unmasked environment variables.

## Copado workflow

Start with `agentia cicd workflow get --json` and honor its value (`local`, `cloud`, or unset).

- **Local:** `list → get → work set → (implement & git commit) → test → publish → submit [--done|--deploy]`
- **Cloud:** `list → get → cloud set → (implement locally and push to the source org) → cloud commit → cloud promote [--deploy]`

Read records before changing them and use IDs returned by Copado. Activate the story (`work set` locally or `cloud set` for cloud) before coding on that path; use one story per feature branch for local Git work. Keep the working tree clean for lifecycle commands, and confirm promotion/deployment intent before `done`.

## Agent Skills

Load exactly one copy of each applicable installed Agentia skill:

- `agentia-cicd`: Copado stories, commits, publish, submit, done, promotions, jobs, Functions, Job Templates, git-hosted extensions, environments, credentials, projects, repositories, pipelines, Org Intelligence metadata explore, metadata index and dependency, Slack notification configure, and data.
- `agentia-testing`: Copado Robotic Testing operations.
- `agentia-ai`: Copado AI operations.
- `agentia-adv`: advanced pipeline workflows.

Project-specific instructions take precedence over managed Agentia skills. Refresh managed skills with `agentia setup skills update`; do not hand-edit managed files.

For CLI upgrades, use `agentia update --check` (or `--check --json` for automation). Self-update runs `npm install --global` only from a global npm install; other layouts need `--force` or the manual npm command printed on failure. Behind TLS-inspecting proxies, `agentia update` retries the version check through `npm view` so npm `cafile`/proxy settings apply. After a successful update, the CLI repairs Agentia `.gitignore` entries in the current project when applicable and warns about outdated MCP *config* entries, legacy `AGENTS.md` sections, and missing Salesforce tooling; run `agentia setup` to apply those fixes interactively. Run `agentia setup skills update` in each project for managed skills, and reload Agentia MCP in your IDE when the CLI warns that older MCP *server processes* are still running, or when an Agentia MCP tool result ends with a notice that a newer version is installed (`--no-refresh` skips the automatic project refresh).
